// `*w += 6` where W: Deref only: E0594, refused (it compiled and RAN). Twin pass/bc_mutplace_derefmut_compound adds the DerefMut impl. Was soundness-queue row derefonly_compound_write_admit (tier 2).
// PROBES.md 2026-09-08a: a place in a mutable-use position takes the DerefMut/IndexMut step at every level, a Deref-only/Index-only step is refused, and the bare `deref_mut()` receiver is asked the binding-mut question.
package bc_mutplace_derefonly_compound_fail;
use logos.lang.ops;
struct W { inner: i64 }
impl Deref<i64> for W { fn deref(&self) -> &i64 { return &self.inner; } }
fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut w: W = W { inner: 1i64 };
    *w += 6i64;
    if w.inner != 7i64 { return 1i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
